{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"c84bd47fda670c4c128973c58657d8aaac3232f9623c1f0f877a9fdb8a7d126e","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[],"case_id":"c9259c8b61e6dddb12bafbb6273d476d715411908f2890d3517e795a176163e2","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[8,8,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[8,8,1]},"entry":"kernel_imageblock_scaled_tile","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"imageblock":{"dimensions":[16,16]},"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"imageblock-scaled-tile-colour-plane","output":{"binding":0,"dimensions":[16,16,1],"kind":"texture","origin":[0,0,0]},"rationale":"A tile twice the threadgroup in each axis: 8x8 threads staging a 2x2 block of imageblock cells each, then copied out as two planes. air.write_imageblock_slice_to_texture_2d.i16.v4f32 (7 case-less corpus sources) and air.write_imageblock_slice_to_texture_2d.i16.f32 (4), 11 sources. Every other authored imageblock case owns one cell per thread, which made the threadgroup extent and the imageblock extent the same number and let three separate places assume it; here the tile is 16x16 and the threadgroup is 8x8, so a lowering that linearised the tile by the threadgroup width lands cells (0,1) and (8,0) on one index and one that took the implicit slice region from the threadgroup extent copies the top-left 8x8 corner of a block Metal copies whole. The colour is (X, Y, X/2, Y/4) and the weight is X + 16Y at cell (X, Y), so each of the 256 cells holds a value that exists nowhere else in the tile, the four colour channels scale differently so a transpose or swizzle lands a quadruple that exists nowhere at all, and the two planes have different widths in the cell so a stride taken from the cell rather than the plane cannot satisfy both; a quarter-sized copy leaves 192 of the 256 texels at their authored poison. Every value is exact in binary32. Both slice regions are implicit, the form that has to derive the extent rather than read it. The dispatch is exactly one 8x8 threadgroup, so exactly one tile exists and the copy has no second threadgroup to race. The 32-byte cell puts 256 of them at 8 KiB, half the threadgroup memory Vulkan guarantees. This case compares the four-channel plane.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[{"binding":0,"dimensions":[16,16,1],"format":"rgba32_float","initial_bytes_b64":"","role":"output","texture_type":"d2"},{"binding":1,"dimensions":[16,16,1],"format":"r32_float","initial_bytes_b64":"","role":"output","texture_type":"d2"}],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
