{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"cae0f85a9fe59869c9f33b1c7d10d596a2108bf754480f68f78d3e29edd99729","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"codex:gpt-5.6-sol","buffers":[{"binding":23,"bytes_b64":"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAQAAAAAAAAABAAAAAAAAAAEAAAAAAAAAAQAAAAAAAAA=","role":"input"},{"binding":29,"initial_bytes_b64":"q6urqw==","role":"in_out"},{"binding":28,"bytes_b64":"AQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAAAAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAQAAAA==","role":"input"}],"case_id":"57e3dd58f7f250b784adef3d133852a2fab86943184d3bb52cbcea16edd4fb73","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[{"binding":0,"elements":[{"bytes_b64":"AACAPw==","index":0,"role":"input"}],"length":1}],"dispatch":{"grid":[1,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[1,1,1]},"entry":"ndArrayCol2im","execution_safety":"authored_bounded","function_constants":[{"bytes_b64":"AQAAAA==","index":122,"scalar_type":"u32"},{"bytes_b64":"AAAAAA==","index":124,"scalar_type":"u32"}],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"linked-single-unit-column-write","output":{"binding":29,"kind":"buffer","length":4,"offset":0},"rationale":"All input, output, kernel, window, dilation, stride, and launched-thread extents are exactly one with zero padding. The channel, window-height, and window-width loops therefore each execute once; the exact linked prefix returns one and the direct destination accumulates that value into the sole poisoned float.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[{"function":"prefixPrimary_f","module_sha256":"02f0c15aa38aa83d7f539616fea75fdd3101b914592aa77a45d75f4b32941e90"}],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"cb5a2178aede0f3f28af50cc4960db0a906ca15851974dd856fd1082867e4d89","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"AAAAAA==","role":"input"}],"case_id":"ab880a84badffd360785e8cae05578b84262d187fec1cb15ebed42d1b654fab4","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"draw":{"instance_count":1,"primitive":"triangle","vertex_count":3,"vertex_start":0},"entry":"read_surf_frag_rg_uint","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"convert-four-uint-texel-pairs-to-half-at-their-own-pixel","output":{"dimensions":[2,2],"index":0,"kind":"render_target","origin":[0,0]},"rationale":"air.convert.f.v2f16.u.v2i32 had no authored case; 43 corpus sources sit behind it. The host reads two unsigned channels of a texel, converts them to half and scales them by half(0.001).\n\nA fragment case cannot choose its varyings, but this shader's only stage-in is air.position, which is the fragment coordinate - the harness cannot move it, and truncating it to uint gives each fragment its own pixel index. So a 2x2 render target over a 2x2 uint texture gives four fragments that each read their own texel, and the case controls all eight numbers.\n\nThe eight are chosen against the two roundings in the path. Every one is exactly representable in half, so the convert itself is not where a difference can hide - what is tested is that the convert happens at all and on the right lanes. The scale then rounds: 1024 and 4096 land exactly on a half, and 2050, 255, 60000, 999 and 7 each round, with the nearest tie at least a quarter of a step away so a one-ULP disagreement between an implementation computing the product at half width and one widening to float cannot change the answer. Zero and 60000 put the pair four binades apart in the same fragment. The two channels the shader does not read hold 0xDEADBEEF and 0xFEEDFACE, so a swizzle that reaches past .rg is visible.\n\nAll thirty-two bytes were derived by hand; Metal and MoltenVK both answer them.","render_targets":[{"dimensions":[2,2],"format":"rgba16_float","index":0,"initial_bytes_b64":"AMcAxwDHAMcAxwDHAMcAxwDHAMcAxwDHAMcAxwDHAMc="}],"samplers":[],"stage":"fragment","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"AAAAAAAEAADvvq3ezvrt/gIIAAAAEAAA776t3s767f7/AAAAYOoAAO++rd7O+u3+5wMAAAcAAADvvq3ezvrt/g==","dimensions":[2,2,1],"format":"rgba32_uint","role":"input","texture_type":"d2"}],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"cb8d0348381db9176c906afd12e794e6b0951df58c6d4b811c578afb907d70d3","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"initial_bytes_b64":"BQAAAPv///8=","role":"in_out"}],"case_id":"c3d4acc16650a832c9b6ec0826529f8edccca884aeeda794b5c4d652307a7a4c","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[1,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[1,1,1]},"entry":"slm_shiftmap_calcminmax1","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"reduce-a-four-by-four-blur-map-into-a-signed-atomic-min-and-max","output":{"binding":0,"kind":"buffer","length":8,"offset":0},"rationale":"Four gathers with offsets (1,1) (1,3) (3,1) (3,3) around pixel (0,0) cover the whole 4x4 texture exactly once, so the reduction is over all sixteen texels and independent of the order gather returns them in. The red channel carries multiples of 1/32 while green and blue carry +9 and -9, so gathering the wrong component misses by four orders of magnitude. The values are, so scaling by 65536 lands on integers and floor/ceil are exact. The extremes sit in opposite corners, so dropping any part of the footprint changes the answer. The min is negative and the max slot starts negative, so an unsigned atomic min or max would leave both slots at their seeds instead of reaching -16384 and 14336.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"ALSASIDIADwAs4BIgMgAPACygEiAyAA8ALGASIDIADwAsIBIgMgAPACugEiAyAA8AKyASIDIADwAqIBIgMgAPAAAgEiAyAA8ACiASIDIADwALIBIgMgAPAAugEiAyAA8ADCASIDIADwAMYBIgMgAPAAygEiAyAA8ADOASIDIADw=","dimensions":[4,4,1],"format":"rgba16_float","role":"input","texture_type":"d2"}],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"cbb81bf9966fd65d89547a0c08a783bd1fed3f5fed852aa456fcdd72d79bf1f1","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"codex:gpt-5.6-sol","buffers":[],"case_id":"fc751c90788701a6188837904d028c8b895aad305813a7ca99371786abdb2ae7","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"draw":{"instance_count":1,"primitive":"triangle","vertex_count":3,"vertex_start":0},"entry":"sphereFrag","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"constant-half-one","output":{"dimensions":[1,1],"index":0,"kind":"render_target","origin":[0,0]},"rationale":"The fragment entry ignores its position input and returns literal half 1.0 at color location zero; one full-coverage fragment must replace the exact poisoned R16Float pixel.","render_targets":[{"dimensions":[1,1],"format":"r16_float","index":0,"initial_bytes_b64":"q6s="}],"samplers":[],"stage":"fragment","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
